completions_1:
A dozen eggs contains twelve eggs. Chatty prepared three dozens of eggs, so she has 3 * 12 = 36 eggs.

She has four children and wants to evenly distribute 36 eggs among them.  To do this, we divide the total number of eggs by the number of children: 36 / 4 = 9 eggs per child.

\boxed{9}

